We are looking for an experienced Quantity Surveyor (QS) – MEP with 8–10 years of relevant experience in commercial projects . The candidate will be responsible for managing the cost and commercial aspects of MEP works, including quantity take-offs, cost estimation, tendering, contract administration, and payment certification. Prepare detailed quantity take-offs, BOQs, and cost estimates for MEP works. Review MEP drawings, specifications, and tender documents to identify scope and quantities. Prepare and evaluate tenders, quotations, and commercial proposals . Manage the cost control and commercial aspects of MEP packages throughout the project lifecycle. Review and verify contractor/subcontractor measurements, invoices, and payment applications. Prepare and evaluate variations, claims, and change orders . Assist in contract administration and ensure compliance with contractual requirements. Monitor project costs, budgets, commitments, and variations. Coordinate with project managers, MEP engineers, consultants, contractors, and procurement teams. Prepare cost reports, financial statements, and commercial updates for management. Support procurement activities and evaluate subcontractor and supplier bids. Maintain accurate records of all commercial and contractual documentation. Identify potential commercial risks and support effective cost management strategies. Required Qualifications & Skills What do we need from you Bachelor's degree in Quantity Surveying, Civil Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering , or a related field. 8–10 years of relevant experience in MEP quantity surveying and cost management. Strong experience in commercial projects such as hotels, hospitals, offices, retail, mixed-use developments, and high-rise buildings. Good knowledge of HVAC, Electrical, Plumbing/PHE, Fire Fighting, and ELV systems . Strong knowledge of BOQ preparation, quantity take-offs, rate analysis, cost estimation, and contract administration . Experience in handling variations, claims, interim payments, and final accounts . Proficiency in MS Excel and relevant quantity surveying/cost management software. Good understanding of construction contracts and commercial practices. What's in it for you? Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering or a related field. 3–6 years of relevant experience in electrical design and engineering. Experience in commercial projects such as hotels, hospitals, offices, retail, mixed-use developments, or high-rise buildings. Proficiency in Auto CAD and knowledge of relevant electrical design software. Good understanding of electrical distribution systems, lighting, power systems, earthing, and ELV systems. Knowledge of relevant electrical codes, standards, and design practices. Good understanding of multidisciplinary coordination. Strong analytical, problem-solving, communication, and coordination skills. Ability to work independently and effectively within a multidisciplinary team. {"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Job Posting","url":"https://jobs.egis-group.com/job/qs-mep-in-gurugram-jid-8257","title":"QS
