About Us Egis is committed to creating an inclusive, creative culture that embraces diversity and flexibility. We offer generous parental leave, support flexible work practices and strive to create an environment where employees can connect, collaborate, grow and succeed. Egis is an organisation with a capacity to make meaningful industry and community change in the space of place-making, sustainability and creating connected cities. Different to other engineering firms, Egis offers true end-to-end capability across the entire design-to-operation lifecycle, offering advisory, architecture, engineering, design, asset management and operations services. We are committed to creating great teams doing innovative work and would love you to join us to Impact the Future. About the Role We are looking for an experienced Project Coordinator with 7–8 years of relevant experience in commercial projects . The candidate will be responsible for coordinating project activities, ensuring effective communication between project stakeholders, monitoring project progress, and supporting the project team in delivering projects within the agreed timelines, budget, and quality standards. What do we need from you Coordinate and monitor day-to-day project activities to ensure smooth project execution. Act as a key point of coordination between clients, consultants, architects, engineers, contractors, and internal project teams . Prepare and maintain project schedules, trackers, progress reports, and project documentation. Monitor project progress against agreed timelines and highlight delays, risks, and critical issues. Organize and coordinate project meetings, prepare agendas, and circulate minutes of meetings (Mo M). Follow up on action items and ensure timely closure of pending tasks. Coordinate the submission and review of drawings, documents, and technical deliverables. Support the project team in managing project deliverables and key milestones. Maintain project records, corresponden